#====================================================================
# Draft knowledge entry - Python 3.12 removes imp/collections.Mapping,
# breaking vendored build-time generators (jinja2 2.8-dev etc.)
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-libfirm-1.22.0-python312-vendored-generators
trigger_tool:           python|make
phase:                  build
error_signature:        "ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'imp'|cannot import name 'Mapping' from 'collections'|Invalid regular expression.*(?u)|re\.compile.*\?u"
severity:               2
category:               build-tool, python, compat, portability, build-system
match_keywords:         python3.12, imp, collections.abc, collections.Mapping, jinja2, markupsafe, code generator, (?u) regex, libfirm
title:                  Python 3.12 removed imp and collections.Mapping — vendored build generators crash; fix with importlib/collections.abc, not by installing packages

root_cause:             Python 3.12 removed the imp module and moved abstract
                        collections (Mapping/MutableMapping) to collections.abc.
                        Old vendored build-time helpers (jinja2 2.8-dev,
                        markupsafe) still do `import imp`,
                        `from collections import Mapping` and use inline regex
                        flag `(?u)` which Python 3.11+ rejects at compile time.
                        The Makefile build then fails inside code generation
                        without any compiler error.

rec_approach:           Patch the vendored helpers minimally in-tree (captured by
                        refresh-patch --auto):
                        1) import imp -> importlib.util (spec_from_file_location);
                        2) from collections import Mapping ->
                           try collections.abc / fallback collections;
                        3) re.compile(r'\w+(?u)') -> re.compile(r'\w+', re.UNICODE).
                        Do NOT pip-install newer jinja2: the vendored copy shadows
                        the system one and CI is a clean environment.

verification_cmd:       python3 scripts/gen_ir.py scripts/ir_spec.py scripts/templates/nodes.h > /dev/null
verification:           After the 3 in-tree fixes libfirm 1.22.0 generation produced
                        valid build/gen/include/libfirm/nodes.h (4316 lines) and
                        make completed; before the fixes it failed with
                        ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'imp'.

affected_scope:         Projects bundling Python-2-era Jinja2/MarkupSafe or using
                        imp in code generators, built with system Python >= 3.10.

forbid_1_pattern:       pip install.*jinja2.*build|replace.*vendored.*jinja2.*wholesale
forbid_1_reason:        Vendored copies are picked first; replacing wholesale changes
                        generated output and reproducibility.
forbid_1_consequence:   Non-reproducible generated headers, hidden behavior changes.

similar_to:             [E339]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

